From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] audio: the sound on its own real-time thread (HDA DMA, mixer)

What: with OMACVM_AUDIO_THREAD=1 the HDA codec's DMA timers and the
mixer's audio timer run as ticks on one thread of their own
(audio/audio-rt.c, "omacvm-audio"), every 1 ms at macOS's time-constraint
policy (user-interactive QoS if refused), instead of in QEMU's main loop.
The thread never takes the BQL. One recursive lock, audio_rt_lock(),
guards what the ticks touch: the mixer (every audio_be_* call takes it),
the HDA codec's streams and the HDA controller's stream registers (its
MMIO handlers take it). Lock order: BQL, audio lock, a backend's own lock.
On the thread the controller's DMA goes straight to guest RAM under RCU
(anything that is not RAM fails the transfer instead of taking the BQL),
and its buffer-completion interrupt is raised from a bottom half. While
the main loop holds the BQL for more than 10 ms (virgl compiling shaders),
a vCPU that leaves the guest waits for it and the guest's PipeWire may not
run: then the stream's clock pauses for that tick (as with a stalled main
loop before) and QEMU's own buffer plays on; afterwards it refills 1/8
faster than real time (1/32 before). main_loop_bql_busy_ns() (util/
main-loop.c, from the stall watchdog's timestamps) says how long the main
loop has held the BQL. The thread sleeps while no stream runs or the VM
is stopped. qemu.log: "OmacVM: sound: own audio thread, <policy>, every
1000 us". Without the variable nothing changes (the lock is a no-op).
OMACVM_AUDIO_BQL_PAUSE_MS, OMACVM_AUDIO_REFILL_DIV and
OMACVM_AUDIO_THREAD_PERIOD_US are for measurements.

Why: the main loop also runs the VM's GPU (virgl) and competes with every
vCPU for the Mac's cores. Each time it ran late, the sound card's DMA and
the mixer stopped, QEMU's 93 ms ring drained, and refilled at 1/32 of real
time: stalls in a row (an app opening, a page scrolling) added up to a
break. On its own thread the sound no longer waits for the GPU.

Applies after qemu-hda-no-catch-up.patch, qemu-main-loop-stall-watchdog.patch
and the SDL audio patches.
Upstream: not sent (OmacVM only for now; the env switch is ours).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/audio (measure.sh, glitches.py), the audio lane's
notes (work/tracks/audio-crackle.md, 2026-10-16) have the runs;
src/tests/audio-timing.sh checks the wiring.

